  "text": {
    "markdown": "## Monthly spending breakdown\n\n**Total: $3,300 a month.** Rent takes more than half of it.\n\n| Category | Amount | Share | |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Rent | $1,800 | 54.5% | `██████████████████████` |\n| Groceries | $520 | 15.8% | `██████` |\n| Dining out | $340 | 10.3% | `████` |\n| Transport | $210 | 6.4% | `███` |\n| Other | $195 | 5.9% | `██` |\n| Utilities | $160 | 4.8% | `██` |\n| Subscriptions | $75 | 2.3% | `█` |\n| **Total** | **$3,300** | **100%** | |\n\nEach block is about 2.5% of the total.\n\n### What the numbers say\n\n- **Rent dominates:** $1,800 is 54.5% of spending, more than everything else combined ($1,500).\n- **Food is the second-biggest area:** groceries and dining out together come to $860, or 26.1%. Dining out alone ($340) is about two-thirds of what you spend on groceries.\n- **Essentials vs everything else:** rent, groceries, transport and utilities add up to $2,690 (81.5%). Dining out, subscriptions and \"other\" make up the flexible $610 (18.5%).\n- **Subscriptions are small:** $75 is 2.3%. Cancelling all of them would save less than cutting dining out by a quarter ($85).\n\n### If you want to cut back\n\nThe realistic levers are **dining out** ($340) and **other** ($195): together $535 a month. Trimming both by 30% frees up about $160 a month, or $1,926 a year, without touching the essentials. Rent is the only category where a change would move the total a lot, and it is the hardest to change.\n",
    "validation": {
      "valid": true,
      "checks": [
        "is non-empty Markdown",
        "contains no raw HTML outside code (react-markdown would print it literally)"
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "warnings": []
